    {
      "id": "82e39ac2f3c99d4d88b95aedc6b879212dd05b71",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1230987591,
          "type": null,
          "body": "@guyharris - your change https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/2686/ - added ui/exit_codes.h and tried not to change existing codes.\n\nDo you object to this change that makes the error codes in that file unique (rather than all 2)?  The motivation was to find a simple way to check whether a display filter is valid using tshark.  dftest only seems to exit with 1 on failure (either hardcoded 1 or EXIT_FAILURE from stdlib.h).  This could also be fixed up to use exit_codes.h to separate INVALID_FILTER from other error cases.\n\nMy hope is that anyone who writes scripts using these processes mostly only checks for 0 for success and so wouldn't be affected by this change.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
